# shell: desktop
# work: home
# PVK-038: the Delete key, which this shell did not have at all.  What it
# means depends on where the item is: a move that can be undone where there
# is a Trash, and a deletion when Shift says the user has decided.
note Delete moves the selection to the Trash rather than destroying it
click-row 1
wait 3
key Delete
wait 30
expect-no-file /tmp/trk_home/.trk-shell-fixture/a.txt
expect-file /tmp/trk_home/.Trash/a.txt
note Shift+Delete is final, and says so
click-row 1
wait 3
key Delete shift
wait 30
expect-no-file /tmp/trk_home/.trk-shell-fixture/b.txt
note and it is not in the Trash either, which is the whole difference
expect-no-file /tmp/trk_home/.Trash/b.txt
quit
